<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/17th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Sarhu</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1619">1619</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Battle of Sarhū</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Sarhu was a series of engagements in 1619 in which <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nurhaci">Nurhaci</a>'s Later Jin army defeated a Ming expedition sent in four columns to destroy his state. Concentrating his forces, Nurhaci beat the columns one by one in a few days. The victory confirmed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jurchens">Jurchen</a> power in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manchuria">Manchuria</a> and opened the way to the conquest of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liaodong">Liaodong</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-sarhu.jpg" alt="Battle of Sarhu" width="320" height="268" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Minggunbattle.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
